{"archetypes":[{"name":"sibling-contract","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan modifies two .sh scripts but the file list omits the required .md sibling updates mandated by script-md-siblings.md for any behavior change in skills/*/scripts/.","prompt_body":"Check whether the plan's file list is complete with respect to the script-md-siblings.md repo rule, which requires sibling .md files to be updated in the same PR as any behavior change to a .sh script under skills/*/scripts/. The plan adds a new warning breadcrumb and removes a function from upgrade-larch.sh, and adds a new test scenario to test-upgrade-larch-prune.sh — verify whether skills/upgrade-larch/scripts/upgrade-larch.md and skills/upgrade-larch/scripts/test-upgrade-larch-prune.md need corresponding updates and whether the plan includes them. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"counter-sync","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan inserts the post-loop overflow warning using ${#SANITIZED_VERSIONS[@]} while the while-loop exit condition uses VERSION_COUNT; the plan does not verify these stay equal at the insertion point under the PRUNE_FAILED_VERSIONS accumulation path.","prompt_body":"Trace the cap-trim loop in upgrade-larch.sh (lines 344–388) and verify that VERSION_COUNT and ${#SANITIZED_VERSIONS[@]} are guaranteed equal when the while loop exits with REMOVED_VERSION=false, specifically when PRUNE_FAILED_VERSIONS has accumulated entries that caused every candidate version to be skipped. Check whether the plan's proposal to test ${#SANITIZED_VERSIONS[@]} (rather than VERSION_COUNT) at the post-loop insertion point is correct or whether a divergence between the two is possible in any exit path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-pin-completeness","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's all-pinned test scenario does not explicitly account for the implicit INSTALLED_VERSION pin appended to ACTIVE_SESSION_VERSIONS at upgrade-larch.sh line 314, making the fixture underdetermined.","prompt_body":"Examine how the prune path builds ACTIVE_SESSION_VERSIONS in upgrade-larch.sh (lines 304–316): INSTALLED_VERSION (basename of PLUGIN_ROOT) is always appended regardless of SESSION_PINNED_VERSIONS, and LATEST_STABLE is exempted by the loop guard at line 350 rather than via ACTIVE_SESSION_VERSIONS. Verify whether the plan's proposed all-pinned test fixture, which must have more than 8 cached versions with zero evictable candidates, correctly accounts for these two implicit preservation paths when selecting PLUGIN_ROOT_VERSION, INSTALL_RESULT_VERSION, and SESSION_PINNED_VERSIONS values, and whether the resulting scenario actually exercises the new cap-overflow warning rather than normal trim or the no-prune branch. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
